    "repo": "swesmith/mozilla__bleach.73871d76",
    "problem_statement": "nofollow callback not working correctly for http URLs\n\n#### Description\n\nThe nofollow callback is not adding the `rel=\"nofollow\"` attribute to http URLs. It seems like the callback is only working for mailto links now, but regular http/https URLs are not getting the nofollow attribute added.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport bleach\nfrom bleach.callbacks import nofollow\n\n# Test with a simple http URL\nhtml = '<a href=\"http://example.com\">Example</a>'\nresult = bleach.linkify(html, callbacks=[nofollow])\nprint(f\"Result: {result}\")\n# Expected: <a href=\"http://example.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">Example</a>\n# Actual: <a href=\"http://example.com\">Example</a>\n\n# Test with linkify function directly\ntext = \"Check out http://example.com\"\nresult = bleach.linkify(text)\nprint(f\"Linkify result: {result}\")\n# Expected: Check out <a href=\"http://example.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://example.com</a>\n# Actual: Check out <a href=\"http://example.com\">http://example.com</a>\n```\n\nThe nofollow attribute is missing from http URLs but seems to work fine for mailto links."
  }
